# Runtime Image Build — `rfipconfig-be` (Shipwright PoC)

Builds the **.NET runtime image** for `rfipconfig-be` using Builds for Red Hat
OpenShift (Shipwright), following the pattern proven on the builder image
build. This is the second of two image builds required before the build
pipeline task (Tekton triggers, Jenkins/Argo + BuildRun + Argo CD) begins.

**Migration requirements implemented here:**

1. Base image pulled from `quay.hobbylobby.corp` (not the legacy `hl-images` namespace)
2. Entrypoint script extracted from the legacy base64-encoded variable into a
   real, version-controlled file (`entrypoint.sh`)
3. Registry credentials handled via a Kubernetes Secret (`pipeline-push-secret`),
   never via environment variables

---

## Why `buildah-hl` and not S2I or the built-in `buildah`

| Strategy | Why not / why |
|----------|---------------|
| `s2i` (custom, used for builder image) | Needs the `s2i-generate` step to compile source. The runtime image has **no source to compile** — wrong tool. |
| `buildah` (built-in, operator-installed) | Correct build type (Dockerfile), but does **not** mount our internal CA → pulls from `quay.hobbylobby.corp` fail with x509. |
| **`buildah-hl` (custom, this repo)** | Copy of the `buildah` step from `s2i.yaml`, keeping the `hobbylobby.corp` CA configMap mount that `SSL_CERT_FILE` points at. ✅ |

