## Steps

### Step 1 — Commit the runtime image content to Git

```bash
mkdir -p runtime-image/
# 1a. Add Dockerfile from this repo; set FROM to the quay base image
# 1b. Extract the entrypoint script from the legacy base64 variable:
echo "<BASE64_VALUE>" | base64 -d > runtime-image/entrypoint.sh
# 1c. Review entrypoint.sh for embedded secrets BEFORE committing
git add runtime-image/ && git commit -m "Add runtime image Dockerfile + entrypoint" && git push
```

### Step 2 — Apply the ClusterBuildStrategy (cluster-admin required)

```bash
oc apply -f buildah-hl.yaml
oc get clusterbuildstrategy buildah-hl        # must exist before Step 3
```

> Only cluster administrators have write access to ClusterBuildStrategy
> resources — namespace-level edit rights are not enough.

### Step 3 — Apply the Build

```bash
oc apply -f rfipconfig-be-runtime.yaml
oc get builds.shipwright.io rfipconfig-be-runtime-image -n openshift-builds \
  -o jsonpath='{.status.reason}'               # expected: Succeeded (= registered)
```

> `Succeeded` here means the Build **definition is valid** (strategy found,
> secrets found, git URL reachable) — not that an image was built yet.
> Always use `builds.shipwright.io`; bare `oc get build` resolves to the
> legacy `build.openshift.io` type.

### Step 4 — Run the BuildRun

```bash
oc create -f buildrun-runtime.yaml             # create, NOT apply (generateName)
oc get buildruns.shipwright.io -n openshift-builds -w
```

The BuildRun creates a TaskRun, which creates the pod that executes the
strategy steps.

### Step 5 — Verify

```bash
oc get pods -n openshift-builds -w             # pod STATUS → Completed
oc get tr -n openshift-builds                  # TaskRun SUCCEEDED → True
oc get buildruns.shipwright.io -n openshift-builds   # SUCCEEDED → True
oc logs -f <buildrun-pod> -n openshift-builds --all-containers
oc get istag -n openshift-builds | grep rfipconfig-be-runtime
```

**Success checklist:**

- [ ] `step-buildah` log: pull from `quay.hobbylobby.corp/...` with **no x509 error**
- [ ] `[INFO] Pushing image ...` completes without `authentication required`
- [ ] BuildRun `SUCCEEDED=True`
- [ ] `istag` shows the `rfipconfig-be-runtime` tag
- [ ] Verified via **CLI only** — console BuildRun detail page still crashes
      (OCPBUGS-84214, operator v1.8.1)

> Pod briefly showing `NotReady` mid-run is expected (a container finished its
> task). If the run fails, read `status.failureDetails` on the BuildRun to see
> the exact pod/container where it failed.

